    },
    {
      "line": 18,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "scene 025.1 — morning after applicator invasion"
    },
    {
      "line": 20,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "scene meta:"
    },
    {
      "line": 21,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "location: Slave Dormitory Caverns / Main Compound Level"
    },
    {
      "line": 22,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "time: year 17,503 (Morning after the Applicator invasion)"
    },
    {
      "line": 23,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "participants: The Nameless One, The Five (hive-linked), Mika, freed slaves, solitary Anunnaki Overseer"
    },
    {
      "line": 24,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "focus: Geralt awakens to find physical chains and overseers gone, but the Five are synchronized hive-puppets; under the Applicator's internal compulsion, Geralt commands the Five to begin excavating the eastern compound section while Mika develops refined gesture-language among the slaves."
    },
    {
      "line": 25,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "continuity: Immediately follows scene 024.11"
    },
    {
      "line": 26,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "presentation: playable-cutscene"
    },
    {
      "line": 27,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "cutscene purpose: Establish the post-evacuation status of the compound, the Five's hive puppeting, and the dual tracks of Geralt's possession and Mika's leadership."
    },
    {
      "line": 29,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Scene One: The Morning After"
    },
    {
      "line": 31,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The nameless one woke to silence."
    },
    {
      "line": 33,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not the oppressive silence of fear or exhaustion, but absence—the specific void created when expected sounds fail to manifest."
    },
    {
      "line": 34,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No chains clanking against stone."
    },
    {
      "line": 35,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No Overseers barking commands."
    },
    {
      "line": 36,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No whips cracking flesh."
    },
    {
      "line": 37,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No screams."
    },
    {
      "line": 39,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His eye throbbed where the thing had entered."
    },
    {
      "line": 40,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not pain, exactly."
    },
    {
      "line": 41,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "More like presence—a weight behind the socket that had no physical mass but occupied space nonetheless."
    },
    {
      "line": 42,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "When he tried to touch it, his fingers found only unmarked skin and the slight dampness of dried tears."
    },
    {
      "line": 44,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But it was there."
    },
    {
      "line": 45,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Inside."
    },
    {
      "line": 46,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Sharing."
    },
    {
      "line": 48,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "What did you do to me?"
    },
    {
      "line": 50,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No answer came."
    },
    {
      "line": 51,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Just that persistent weight, that sense of something coiled around his optic nerve, tendrils spreading through neural pathways with patient inevitability."
    },
    {
      "line": 53,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Nameless one pushed himself upright, muscles protesting."
    },
    {
      "line": 54,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Around him, the dormitory was stirring with unusual lethargy."
    },
    {
      "line": 55,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Slaves rose slowly, confused by the absence of Overseers forcing them to their feet, uncertain whether this change meant improvement or new horror they hadn't yet recognized."
    },
    {
      "line": 57,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The five sat in their protective circle around where he'd been lying."
    },
    {
      "line": 58,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But something was wrong with them."
    },
    {
      "line": 60,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They moved in perfect synchronization."
    },
    {
      "line": 62,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "All five turned their heads toward him simultaneously."
    },
    {
      "line": 63,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "All five blinked at exactly the same moment."
    },
    {
      "line": 64,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "All five rose to their feet with movements so identical they might have been reflections in parallel mirrors."
    },
    {
      "line": 66,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Their eyes met his—not with the desperate hope or fragile trust they'd shown before, but with empty expectation."
    },
    {
      "line": 67,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Waiting."
    },
    {
      "line": 68,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Ready to receive commands they hadn't been given."
    },
    {
      "line": 70,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Nameless one's stomach lurched."
    },
    {
      "line": 72,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No."
    },
    {
      "line": 73,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No, what have I done to them?"
    },
    {
      "line": 74,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "What has IT done?"
    },
    {
      "line": 76,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He raised his hand, making the question gesture—palm up, fingers curled, three short movements."
    },
    {
      "line": 77,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(Are you alright?)"
    },
    {
      "line": 79,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They responded with synchronized nods, then the affirmation gesture—fist to chest, single sharp motion."
    },
    {
      "line": 80,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Their movements matched so perfectly they might have been controlled by single consciousness."
    },
    {
      "line": 81,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(Yes."
    },
    {
      "line": 82,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "We obey.)"
    },
    {
      "line": 84,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Cold horror crawled up The Nameless one's spine."
    },
    {
      "line": 85,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "These weren't the individuals who had protected him, who had formed their constellation of desperate alliance."
    },
    {
      "line": 86,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "These were puppets."
    },
    {
      "line": 87,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Empty vessels waiting to be filled with purpose they couldn't generate themselves."
    },
    {
      "line": 89,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The scarred one—the one who would become Mika—watched from her position just outside the circle."
    },
    {
      "line": 90,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Her eyes were wide, darting between The Nameless one and the five with expression that mixed terror and fascination."
    },
    {
      "line": 91,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She'd seen."
    },
    {
      "line": 92,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Last night, when the five had sat up glowing, she'd witnessed what The Nameless one couldn't remember, couldn't have seen while drowning in his own invasion."
    },
    {
      "line": 94,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She knew something was desperately wrong."
    },
    {
      "line": 96,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But before The Nameless one could gesture to her, could try to understand what she'd witnessed, sounds cut through the dormitory's unusual quiet:"
    },
    {
      "line": 98,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Rhythmic grunts, rising pitch—disbelief-joy-confusion"
    },
    {
      "line": 99,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(Free!"
    },
    {
      "line": 100,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "We're free!)"
    },
    {
      "line": 102,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not the tortured sounds of suffering, but something different—genuine emotion vocalized through the crude communication they'd developed."
    },
    {
      "line": 103,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The sound of beings discovering something so unexpected they couldn't process it without expression."
    },
    {
      "line": 105,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Slaves were gathering near the dormitory's entrance, gesturing wildly, some producing the wet, choking sounds that meant weeping when vocal cords couldn't properly form words."
    },
    {
      "line": 107,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Nameless one moved toward them, the five following with footsteps that matched his rhythm exactly—too exactly, with precision that suggested coordination beyond conscious choice."
    },
    {
      "line": 108,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The scarred one trailed behind, maintaining distance, watching everything with sharp attention that suggested she was cataloging details for later analysis."
    },
    {
      "line": 110,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The entrance opened onto what had been the primary mining level."
    },
    {
      "line": 111,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But it was transformed."
    },
    {
      "line": 113,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The chains were gone."
    },
    {
      "line": 115,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not cut."
    },
    {
      "line": 116,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not broken."
    },
    {
      "line": 117,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Simply absent, as though they'd never existed."
    },
    {
      "line": 118,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The shackles that had connected every slave to the floor had vanished overnight, leaving only faint depressions in stone where metal had rested."
    },
    {
      "line": 120,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Overseers were gone too."
    },
    {
      "line": 121,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No Reptilians prowling with energy whips."
    },
    {
      "line": 122,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No Gruuliths standing like immovable sentinels."
    },
    {
      "line": 123,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No Dregans casting predatory shadows."
    },
    {
      "line": 124,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Just... absence."
    },
    {
      "line": 126,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But the walls remained."
    },
    {
      "line": 127,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The compound was still sealed."
    },
    {
      "line": 128,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And high above, on the observation platform that overlooked the entire complex, a single figure stood in golden magnificence."
    },
    {
      "line": 130,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "One Anunnaki."
    },
    {
      "line": 131,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The last one."
    },
    {
      "line": 132,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Left behind to ensure compliance, to maintain some semblance of authority, to remind the freed slaves that their freedom was conditional upon behavior that pleased powers still vastly greater than themselves."
    },
    {
      "line": 134,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The slaves below stared up at that solitary figure with expressions that ranged from lingering terror to confused gratitude."
    },
    {
      "line": 135,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Stockholm syndrome written across every face that had survived long enough to develop it—the psychological adaptation that made captivity bearable by convincing consciousness that captors were protectors, that slavery was safety, that chains were comfort."
    },
    {
      "line": 137,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Three sharp grunts, hands pressed to chest, fingers spread upward"
    },
    {
      "line": 138,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(They freed us!"
    },
    {
      "line": 139,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Mercy!)"
    },
    {
      "line": 141,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Wet, choking sounds, the weeping-grunt, hands touching bare ankles then reaching toward the golden figure"
    },
    {
      "line": 142,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(Gratitude!"
    },
    {
      "line": 143,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Thank the masters!)"
    },
    {
      "line": 145,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Nameless one felt bile rise in his throat."
    },
    {
      "line": 146,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His hands moved involuntarily, forming the negation gesture—sharp downward slash, aggressive bark."
    },
    {
      "line": 147,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(No!)"
    },
    {
      "line": 149,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But the slaves didn't understand."
    },
    {
      "line": 150,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Or chose not to."
    },
    {
      "line": 151,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They continued their expressions of gratitude toward the being that had enslaved them, Stockholm syndrome so complete they couldn't recognize continued captivity when it lacked overt restraint."
    },
    {
      "line": 153,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Walls, The Nameless one's hands formed the gesture frantically, pointing at the sealed compound boundaries."
    },
    {
      "line": 154,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Still trapped."
    },
    {
      "line": 155,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Still watching."
    },
    {
      "line": 156,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(Walls remain."
    },
    {
      "line": 157,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not free."
    },
    {
      "line": 158,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Still prisoners.)"
    },
    {
      "line": 160,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A few slaves turned to look at him with confusion."
    },
    {
      "line": 161,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Some with resentment—as though his refusal to celebrate their \"liberation\" was ingratitude toward masters who had shown mercy."
    },
    {
      "line": 162,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Others simply turned away, choosing the comfort of delusion over the horror of recognizing their situation hadn't fundamentally changed."
    },
    {
      "line": 164,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No, the spark protested weakly, struggling against the weight pressing down from behind The Nameless one's eye."
    },
    {
      "line": 165,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No, they don't understand."
    },
    {
      "line": 166,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "This isn't—"
    },
    {
      "line": 168,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But then something else rose."
    },
    {
      "line": 169,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Something that wasn't the spark."
    },
    {
      "line": 170,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Something cold and calculating that spoke with voice that was his but wasn't his:"
    },
    {
      "line": 172,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Good."
    },
    {
      "line": 173,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Let them believe they're free."
    },
    {
      "line": 174,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Grateful slaves are compliant slaves."
    },
    {
      "line": 175,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "We can use this."
    },
    {
      "line": 177,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Nameless one's hands clenched involuntarily."
    },
    {
      "line": 178,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His jaw tightened."
    },
    {
      "line": 179,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And when he turned to look at the five standing behind him in their perfect formation, his throat produced sounds and gestures without conscious decision:"
    },
    {
      "line": 181,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Commanding bark, follow-motion, urgent-sharp"
    },
    {
      "line": 182,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(Come."
    },
    {
      "line": 183,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Work."
    },
    {
      "line": 184,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Now.)"
    },
    {
      "line": 186,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The five followed instantly, without question, without hesitation."
    },
    {
      "line": 187,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Their synchronized footsteps echoed through the transformed compound as The Nameless one led them away from the celebrating slaves, away from the scarred one's sharp observation, toward the compound's eastern section where few others had gathered."
    },
    {
      "line": 189,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Why am I doing this?"
    },
    {
      "line": 190,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Where am I going?"
    },
    {
      "line": 191,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "What work?"
    },
    {
      "line": 193,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But his body continued moving with purpose that originated from somewhere behind his eye, from the thing that coiled around his optic nerve, from the presence that had learned his pathways during the night and now tested its capability to direct them."
    },
    {
      "line": 195,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His hands gestured commands he didn't consciously choose:"
    },
    {
      "line": 197,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Point-dig motion, downward spiral"
    },
    {
      "line": 198,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(Excavate here."
    },
    {
      "line": 199,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Deep.)"
    },
    {
      "line": 201,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The five moved to obey, finding crude tools left scattered from the Overseers' departure."
    },
    {
      "line": 202,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They began digging with synchronized efficiency, never questioning why, never asking what purpose this served."
    },
    {
      "line": 204,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Crystal, his hands formed the gesture—fingers spread, light-catching motion."
    },
    {
      "line": 205,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Find crystal."
    },
    {
      "line": 206,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Bring."
    },
    {
      "line": 207,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(Search for crystalline structures."
    },
    {
      "line": 208,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Retrieve them.)"
    },
    {
      "line": 210,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "What crystal?"
    },
    {
      "line": 211,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Where?"
    },
    {
      "line": 212,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Why do I know this?"
    },
    {
      "line": 214,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But his body turned away from the five's work site before the internal questions could manifest as hesitation."
    },
    {
      "line": 215,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He needed to leave."
    },
    {
      "line": 216,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Needed to get away from them before the compulsion to command them grew stronger, before he became completely subsumed in whatever the thing behind his eye was trying to accomplish."
    },
    {
      "line": 218,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He walked back toward the main compound area, where other slaves were exploring their new freedom with tentative steps."
    },
    {
      "line": 219,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And there—organizing groups, using sophisticated gesture-language to convey complex instructions—was the scarred one."
    },
    {
      "line": 221,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She looked up as The Nameless one approached."
    },
    {
      "line": 222,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Her eyes met his with sharp intelligence that had survived everything the mines had tried to grind away."
    },
    {
      "line": 223,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She made the question gesture, layered with concern—palm up, fingers trembling slightly, head tilted."
    },
    {
      "line": 224,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(You—alright?"
    },
    {
      "line": 225,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Different?)"
    },
    {
      "line": 227,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Nameless one felt relief flood through him as the compulsion eased."
    },
    {
      "line": 228,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Away from the five, his thoughts were his own again."
    },
    {
      "line": 229,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His hands moved with genuine intention rather than puppet-string direction:"
    },
    {
      "line": 231,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Two-beat grunt, affirmation-gesture, but weak"
    },
    {
      "line": 232,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(Yes."
    },
    {
      "line": 233,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But... complicated.)"
    },
    {
      "line": 235,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The scarred one's eyes narrowed."
    },
    {
      "line": 236,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She gestured sharply—pointed at the five's distant work site, then at The Nameless one's eye where the thing had entered, then made a gesture they'd developed for wrongness, for danger, for things that violated natural order."
    },
    {
      "line": 237,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(They—controlled?"
    },
    {
      "line": 238,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "You—infected?"
    },
    {
      "line": 239,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Danger?)"
    },
    {
      "line": 241,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Nameless one's hands trembled as he formed the response:"
    },
    {
      "line": 243,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Hesitant grunt, half-gesture of uncertainty"
    },
    {
      "line": 244,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(Don't know."
    },
    {
      "line": 245,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Can't control."
    },
    {
      "line": 246,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Need... help.)"
    },
    {
      "line": 248,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She studied him for long moment, then nodded once with decision that carried weight."
    },
    {
      "line": 249,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Her hands moved with purpose:"
    },
    {
      "line": 251,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Sharp gestures, teaching-motion, communication-symbols"
    },
    {
      "line": 252,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(Teach."
    },
    {
      "line": 253,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Language."
    },
    {
      "line": 254,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Together."
    },
    {
      "line": 255,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Fight it.)"
    },
    {
      "line": 257,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And for the first time since waking, The Nameless one felt something like hope."
    },
    {
      "line": 258,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "line": 259,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Language."
    },
    {
      "line": 260,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Communication more sophisticated than grunts and crude gestures."
    },
    {
      "line": 261,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A way to reach the other slaves, to organize them, to build something that wasn't tainted by the thing controlling the five."
    },
    {
      "line": 263,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He gestured agreement, emphatic and grateful:"
    },
    {
      "line": 265,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Affirmation, alliance, gratitude"
    },
    {
      "line": 266,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "(Yes."
    },
    {
      "line": 267,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Together."
    },
    {
      "line": 268,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Thank you.)"
    },
    {
      "line": 270,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The scarred one's expression softened fractionally—the first hint of the person she would become, the ally who would stand beside him through everything that followed."
    },
    {
      "line": 271,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She turned to the gathered slaves and began demonstrating refined gesture-language, building on the crude communication they'd developed but elevating it toward something approaching true language."
    },
    {
      "line": 273,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And The Nameless one stood there, split between two realities:"
    },
    {
      "line": 275,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Here, with her, teaching and learning and building something real, he felt like himself."
    },
    {
      "line": 276,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The spark burned bright and clean."
    },
    {
      "line": 277,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His thoughts were his own."
    },
    {
      "line": 278,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His hands moved with intention he controlled."
    },
    {
      "line": 280,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But in the distance, the five continued their synchronized excavation, digging toward something The Nameless one's conscious mind couldn't name but his possessed body knew with terrible certainty."
    },
    {
      "line": 282,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The crystalline hut waited in the depths."
    },
    {
      "line": 284,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And the thing behind his eye was patient."
    },
    {
      "line": 286,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It could afford to be."
    },
    {
      "line": 287,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It had time."
    },
    {
      "line": 288,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It had control."
    },
    {
      "line": 289,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And it had discovered that its host was strongest when allowed moments of freedom—moments that made the inevitable return to control all the more devastating by contrast."
    },
    {
      "line": 291,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "This is what it means to be possessed, The Nameless one thought with crystalline clarity as he watched the scarred one teach gesture-language to grateful slaves."
    },
    {
      "line": 292,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not erased."
    },
    {
      "line": 293,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Just... shared."
    },
    {
      "line": 294,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Your mind fractured between who you are and what you're being made to do."
    },
    {
      "line": 296,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And the worst part?"
    },
    {
      "line": 297,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Knowing that somewhere in this compound, five beings you care about are suffering the same fate."
    },
    {
      "line": 298,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Emptied."
    },
    {
      "line": 299,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Hollowed."
    },
    {
      "line": 300,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Waiting for commands from consciousness that isn't their own."
    },
    {
      "line": 302,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The scarred one glanced at him, made questioning gesture."
    },
    {
      "line": 303,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He forced himself to respond with teaching motions, with focus on the present task, with everything except the horror gnawing at him from within."
    },
    {
      "line": 305,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The compound settled into its new routine."
    },
    {
      "line": 306,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Free slaves who didn't understand they remained imprisoned."
    },
    {
      "line": 307,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "An Anunnaki watching from heights with clinical interest."
    },
    {
      "line": 308,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And one consciousness learning that freedom could be condition rather than state—granted in moments, revoked when the thing behind his eye decided work needed doing."
    },
    {
      "line": 310,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The day stretched on."
    },
    {
      "line": 311,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Language lessons continued."
    },
    {
      "line": 312,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And in the eastern section, five slaves dug deeper into earth that hadn't been disturbed since before the Anunnaki came."
    },
    {
      "line": 314,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Excavating something that should have remained buried."
    },
    {
      "line": 316,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Building something that would change everything."
    },
    {
      "line": 318,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Again."
    },
    {
      "line": 320,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 322,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "~Year 17,503 (Days after scene 025.1)"
    }
  ],
